note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note seed/host/execfds/execfds.om: fixture for execfds (keyword 201), program mode, AArch64 Linux.
note r = execfds A off n E eoff en K koff kn: A argv packet, E environment packet (execenv framing), K a
note flat list of little-endian u32 descriptors to keep (kn a multiple of 4, strictly increasing, each in
note 3..2147483647). Stdio 0..2 is always kept; every other descriptor above 2 is closed before execve.
note Run by the OM-2 conductor through seed/host/execfds/execfds.cases from the repository root.
note
note Parent mode (no argument): exit 0 when every check holds, else the number of the first failed check.
note  1 a pipe write end dup'ed to 7 with O_CLOEXEC and kept survives the re-exec; the new image writes
note    "status-ok\n" to 7 while /dev/null at 9 and both original pipe ends are gone (child exit 0)
note  2 the parent reads exactly "status-ok\n" and then end of file: no other write end survived
note  3 two kept descriptors, both opened O_CLOEXEC (7 and 9), survive; nothing else above 2 is open
note  4 the lower bound 3 is a valid kept descriptor; the unlisted 9 is closed
note  5 an empty keep list (kn 0) closes everything above 2
note  6 a failed exec (missing program) returns -2; the listed 7 is still open, the unlisted 9 is closed
note  7 a kept descriptor that is not open (40) returns -9 before anything is closed: 7 and 9 still open
note  8 2147483647 is inside the range (not a trap): not open, so -9
note  9-14 invalid keep lists trap 3 (exit 103): kn 2, kn 5, [9,7], [7,7], [2], [2147483648]
note 15 framing before descriptor checks: [40,7] with 40 closed traps 3 (not -9)
note 16 framing before descriptor checks: an argv packet of count 0 with keep [40] traps 3 (not -9)
note 17-21 malformed packets trap 3: empty first argv record, argv trailing byte, environment count 0,
note    empty second environment record, embedded zero in an environment record
note 22 past the old exec caps: 1100 argv records (one of 65535 bytes, packet over 65536 bytes) and 73
note    environment records (two identical "DUP=1", one of 5004 bytes, packet over 4096 bytes) all reach the
note    child (count mode exit 0)
note 23 the kernel's E2BIG: with RLIMIT_STACK soft 8 MiB (ARG_MAX 2 MiB), 64 records of 65535 bytes give -7
note 24 no cap of execfds's own on the keep list: 1100 kept descriptors 1000..2099 (4400 bytes of K, all
note    O_CLOEXEC) reach the child; 3..999 and 2100..2131 are closed. Needs RLIMIT_NOFILE hard >= 2200
note    (else exit 77, a failure, never a skip).
note 25 control: under a self-set RLIMIT_AS soft 16 MiB, a valid 4 MiB argv packet (missing program, 64
note    records of 65535 bytes) needs its own decode mapping, which the kernel refuses: -12 (ENOMEM)
note 26-29 framing before any mapping, under the same cap: the same packet with one trailing byte (26), with a
note    zero byte in its last record (27), with an empty first record (28), and the valid packet with an
note    environment [A=1, ""] (29) each trap 3 (exit 103), never -12: a malformed packet costs only the reading
note    of its bytes (each one kills the omc.om mutant that drops that check from the validation pass)
note Child modes (argv[1]): child FD... (exactly FD... open among 3..max(19, last+16): exit 0, 60 a listed
note fd closed, 61 an unlisted fd open, 62 bad argument), status FD (as child, then writes "status-ok\n" to FD,
note 63 short write), count NA NE (70 argcnt, 71 envcnt, 72 duplicate entries, 73 long entry, 74 long arg),
note range LO HI (60/61 as child), report MAX (prints argv lengths, environment and fd 0..MAX states).
note Other modes: fault (exit 38 when execfds returns -38 with 7 still open; 50 when it executed; 39 when 7
note was lost), packets S / launch S (oracle parity scenarios 1..6 for seed/host/execfds/oracle.py),
note order (one direct execfds for the strace order check in seed/host/execfds/check.sh), and three runs
note for the strace memory check there: malbig (a 4 MiB argv packet with one trailing byte: trap 3, no
note mapping), lying (a 9-byte environment packet whose count field says 65535: trap 3, no mapping) and bigok
note (the valid 4 MiB packet with a missing program: prints "bytes N M K", the packet and keep-list sizes, then exit 0
note when execfds returned -2; its mappings are bounded against N and M by seed/host/execfds/oracle.py).
om2
text cmode "child"
text smode "status"
text nmode "count"
text gmode "range"
text rmode "report"
text fmode "fault"
text pmode "packets"
text lmode "launch"
text omode "order"
text snapmode "snapshot"
text mbmode "malbig"
text lymode "lying"
text bomode "bigok"
text sbytes "bytes "
text devnull "/dev/null"
text fdinfo "/proc/self/fdinfo/"
text missing "/nonexistent/omega-execfds-missing"
text okmsg "status-ok\n"
text dupe "DUP=1"
text aone "A=1"
text bigname "BIG="
text sopen " open\n"
text sclosed " closed\n"
text sfd "fd "
text sresult "result -"
text sargc "argc "
text sarg "arg "
text senvc "envc "
text senv "env "
text sp " "
text nl "\n"
global pa uchar 4400000
global pe uchar 16384
global pk uchar 8192
global buf uchar 70000
global num uchar 32
global rb uchar 64
global path uchar 64
global pb uchar 8
global lim uchar 32
global status uchar 4
global ac ulong 1
global ap ulong 1
global ec ulong 1
global ep ulong 1
global kp ulong 1
global ln ulong 3

note ---- decimal and output ----------------------------------------------------------------------
note decimal digits of v into num; returns their count
fn dec v ulong to ulong
x = v
k = ulong 0
while ge x 10 bound 32
put rb k uchar add 48 rem x 10
x = div x 10
k = add k 1
end
put rb k uchar add 48 x
k = add k 1
for i ulong k
put num i get rb sub sub k i 1
end
ret k
end
fn wt s view uchar * to void
r = write 1 s 0 len s
end
fn wn v ulong to void
n = dec v
r = write 1 num 0 n
end
fn wb n ulong to void
r = write 1 buf 0 n
end

note ---- argv packet pa (count ac, position ap) -------------------------------------------------
fn aini to void
put ac 0 0
put ap 0 2
end
fn abyte b ulong to void
put pa get ap 0 uchar b
put ap 0 add get ap 0 1
end
fn ahdr n ulong to void
abyte and n 255
abyte shr n 8
put ac 0 add get ac 0 1
end
fn atext s view uchar * to void
ahdr len s
for i ulong len s
abyte ulong get s i
end
end
fn arep b ulong n ulong to void
ahdr n
for i ulong n
abyte b
end
end
fn anum v ulong to void
n = dec v
ahdr n
for i ulong n
abyte ulong get num i
end
end
note argv0 exactly as this process was started
fn aself to void
n = argread 0 buf 0 len buf
if le n 0
exit 90
end
ahdr ulong n
for i ulong ulong n
abyte ulong get buf i
end
end
fn afin to ulong
put pa 0 uchar and get ac 0 255
put pa 1 uchar shr get ac 0 8
ret get ap 0
end

note ---- environment packet pe (count ec, position ep) ------------------------------------------
fn eini to void
put ec 0 0
put ep 0 2
end
fn ebyte b ulong to void
put pe get ep 0 uchar b
put ep 0 add get ep 0 1
end
fn ehdr n ulong to void
ebyte and n 255
ebyte shr n 8
put ec 0 add get ec 0 1
end
fn etext s view uchar * to void
ehdr len s
for i ulong len s
ebyte ulong get s i
end
end
note n distinct entries "XAB=" (names XAA, XAB, ... over 26 x 26)
fn emany n ulong to void
for i ulong n
ehdr 4
ebyte 88
ebyte add 65 div i 26
ebyte add 65 rem i 26
ebyte 61
end
end
note one entry "BIG=" followed by n bytes 'b'
fn ebig n ulong to void
ehdr add len bigname n
for i ulong len bigname
ebyte ulong get bigname i
end
for i ulong n
ebyte 98
end
end
fn efin to ulong
put pe 0 uchar and get ec 0 255
put pe 1 uchar shr get ec 0 8
ret get ep 0
end

note ---- keep list pk -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn kini to void
put kp 0 0
end
fn kadd v ulong to void
p = get kp 0
for i ulong 4
put pk add p i uchar and shr v mul i 8 255
end
put kp 0 add p 4
end
fn klen to ulong
ret get kp 0
end

note ---- descriptors --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note is fd open: /proc/self/fdinfo/FD opens (the probe descriptor is closed again at once)
fn isopen fd ulong to bool
n = dec fd
for i ulong len fdinfo
put path i get fdinfo i
end
for i ulong n
put path add len fdinfo i get num i
end
f = fopen path 0 add len fdinfo n 524288 0
if lt f 0
ret false
end
c = fclose int f
ret true
end
note /dev/null at descriptor t with dup3 flags fl (0 or O_CLOEXEC 524288)
fn nullat t int fl int to void
f = fopen devnull 0 len devnull 524288 0
if lt f 0
exit 97
end
if eq f long t
ret
end
r = dupfd int f t fl
if lt r 0
exit 97
end
c = fclose int f
end
fn dupout t int fl int to void
r = dupfd 1 t fl
if lt r 0
exit 97
end
end
note close 3..64 so that inherited descriptors never enter a comparison
fn clean to void
for i ulong 62
c = fclose int add i 3
end
end
fn rd32 o ulong to ulong
v = ulong 0
for i ulong 4
v = or v shl ulong get pb add o i mul i 8
end
ret v
end
fn g64 o ulong to ulong
v = ulong 0
for i ulong 8
v = or v shl ulong get lim add o i mul i 8
end
ret v
end
fn p64 o ulong v ulong to void
for i ulong 8
put lim add o i uchar and shr v mul i 8 255
end
end
note raise the soft limit of resource res to its hard limit; exit 77 when the hard limit is below need
fn raise res int need ulong to void
r = prlimit 0 res lim 0 16
if ne r 0
exit 77
end
h = g64 8
if lt h need
exit 77
end
p64 0 h
p64 8 h
r = prlimit 0 res lim 0 32
if ne r 0
exit 77
end
end
fn reap pid long to ulong
r = waitpid int pid status 0 len status 0
if ne r pid
ret 1000
end
if ne get status 0 0
ret 2000
end
ret ulong get status 1
end

note ---- argument parsing ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn argnum i ulong to ulong
n = argread i buf 0 len buf
if le n 0
exit 62
end
if gt n 10
exit 62
end
v = ulong 0
for j ulong ulong n
c = get buf j
if lt c 48
exit 62
end
if gt c 57
exit 62
end
v = add mul v 10 ulong sub c 48
end
ret v
end
fn argis i ulong s view uchar * to bool
n = argread i buf 0 len buf
if ne n long len s
ret false
end
for j ulong len s
if ne get buf j get s j
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note is fd one of the decimal arguments from index 2 on
fn listed fd ulong to bool
c = ulong argcnt
for i ulong sub c 2
if eq argnum add i 2 fd
ret true
end
end
ret false
end

note ---- child modes ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn childm to int
c = ulong argcnt
prev = ulong 2
for i ulong sub c 2
v = argnum add i 2
if le v prev
ret 62
end
if not isopen v
ret 60
end
prev = v
end
top = add prev 16
if lt top 19
top = ulong 19
end
for j ulong sub top 2
f = add j 3
if isopen f
if not listed f
ret 61
end
end
end
ret 0
end
fn statusm to int
if ne argcnt 3
ret 62
end
s = childm
if ne s 0
ret s
end
w = write int argnum 2 okmsg 0 len okmsg
if ne w long len okmsg
ret 63
end
ret 0
end
fn countm to int
if lt argcnt 4
ret 62
end
na = argnum 2
nv = argnum 3
if ne ulong argcnt na
ret 70
end
if ne ulong envcnt nv
ret 71
end
for e ulong 2
n = envread e buf 0 len buf
if ne n long len dupe
ret 72
end
for j ulong len dupe
if ne get buf j get dupe j
ret 72
end
end
end
n = envread 2 buf 0 len buf
if ne n 5004
ret 73
end
n = argread sub na 1 buf 0 len buf
if ne n 65535
ret 74
end
ret 0
end
fn rangem to int
if ne argcnt 4
ret 62
end
lo = argnum 2
hi = argnum 3
for j ulong sub lo 3
if isopen add j 3
ret 61
end
end
for j ulong add sub hi lo 1
if not isopen add lo j
ret 60
end
end
for j ulong 32
if isopen add add hi 1 j
ret 61
end
end
ret 0
end
fn fdlines top ulong to void
for f ulong add top 1
wt sfd
wn f
if isopen f
wt sopen
else
wt sclosed
end
end
end
fn reportm to int
if lt argcnt 3
ret 62
end
top = argnum 2
c = ulong argcnt
wt sargc
wn c
wt nl
for i ulong c
n = argread i buf 0 len buf
wt sarg
wn i
wt sp
wn ulong n
wt nl
end
e = ulong envcnt
wt senvc
wn e
wt nl
for i ulong e
n = envread i buf 0 len buf
wt senv
wn i
wt sp
wb ulong n
wt nl
end
fdlines top
ret 0
end

note ---- launches ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note kind 1: 7 = stdout (O_CLOEXEC), 9 = /dev/null; kind 2: 7 and 9 = /dev/null, both O_CLOEXEC;
note kind 3: 3 and 9 = /dev/null
fn prep kind ulong to void
if eq kind 1
dupout 7 524288
nullat 9 0
end
if eq kind 2
nullat 7 524288
nullat 9 524288
end
if eq kind 3
nullat 3 0
nullat 9 0
end
end
note fork; the child prepares descriptors and calls execfds with the current packets; 98 if it returns
fn tryl kind ulong an ulong en ulong kn ulong to ulong
pid = fork
if lt pid 0
ret 1001
end
if eq pid 0
prep kind
r = execfds pa 0 an pe 0 en pk 0 kn
exit 98
end
ret reap pid
end
note fork; execfds must return want, then 7 must be open and 9 open (open9) or closed
fn tryr an ulong en ulong kn ulong want long open9 bool to ulong
pid = fork
if lt pid 0
ret 1001
end
if eq pid 0
prep 1
r = execfds pa 0 an pe 0 en pk 0 kn
if ne r want
exit 1
end
if not isopen 7
exit 2
end
if open9
if not isopen 9
exit 3
end
else
if isopen 9
exit 3
end
end
exit 0
end
ret reap pid
end
fn envone to ulong
eini
etext aone
ret efin
end
note argv [self, "child", fds...] for one or two descriptors (b 0: only a)
fn achild a ulong b ulong to ulong
aini
aself
atext cmode
if ne a 0
anum a
end
if ne b 0
anum b
end
ret afin
end
fn faultm to int
pid = fork
if lt pid 0
ret 51
end
if eq pid 0
prep 1
an = achild 7 0
en = envone
kini
kadd 7
r = execfds pa 0 an pe 0 en pk 0 klen
if not isopen 7
ret 39
end
ret int and ulong neg r 255
end
s = reap pid
if eq s 0
ret 50
end
ret int s
end

note ---- oracle parity scenarios (seed/host/execfds/oracle.py builds the same descriptors itself) ------
note 1 keep [7]; 2 keep []; 3 big (1100 args, 73 entries, keep 7 and 1000..2099); 4 missing program, keep
note [7]; 5 keep [7,40] (40 closed); 6 keep [9,7] (trap). argv [self or missing, "report", MAX];
note environment [DUP=1, DUP=1, A=1] (scenario 3: DUP=1, DUP=1, BIG=..., 70 distinct).
fn scen s ulong to void
top = ulong 24
if eq s 3
top = ulong 2131
end
aini
if eq s 4
atext missing
else
aself
end
atext rmode
anum top
if eq s 3
for i ulong 1096
arep 120 1
end
arep 121 65535
end
put ln 0 afin
eini
etext dupe
etext dupe
if eq s 3
ebig 5000
emany 70
else
etext aone
end
put ln 1 efin
kini
if eq s 6
kadd 9
end
if ne s 2
kadd 7
end
if eq s 3
for i ulong 1100
kadd add 1000 i
end
end
if eq s 5
kadd 40
end
put ln 2 klen
end
fn wfull a ulong to void
n = get ln a
for i ulong 8
put rb i uchar and shr n mul i 8 255
end
r = write 1 rb 0 8
d = ulong 0
w = long 0
while lt d n bound 9223372036854775807
if eq a 0
w = write 1 pa d sub n d
else
if eq a 1
w = write 1 pe d sub n d
else
w = write 1 pk d sub n d
end
end
if le w 0
exit 96
end
d = add d ulong w
end
end
fn packetm to int
s = argnum 2
scen s
wfull 0
wfull 1
wfull 2
ret 0
end
fn launchm to int
s = argnum 2
clean
prep 1
if eq s 3
raise 7 2200
for i ulong 1100
dupout int add 1000 i 524288
end
end
scen s
r = execfds pa 0 get ln 0 pe 0 get ln 1 pk 0 get ln 2
wt sresult
wn ulong neg r
wt nl
fdlines 24
ret 0
end
note snapshot: expose caller K=[7] through one 4-byte write (ptrace captures its buffer address), then
note launch scenario 1. snapshot.py changes caller K to [9] at unshare return and observes kept/closed fds.
fn snapm to int
clean
prep 1
scen 1
r = write 1 pk 0 4
if ne r 4
ret 97
end
r = execfds pa 0 get ln 0 pe 0 get ln 1 pk 0 get ln 2
ret 98
end
fn orderm to int
clean
prep 1
an = achild 7 0
en = envone
kini
kadd 7
r = execfds pa 0 an pe 0 en pk 0 klen
ret 98
end

note ---- memory modes ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note argv [program, 64 records of 65535 bytes]: the program is argv0 (self) or the missing path
fn bigargv self bool to ulong
aini
if self
aself
else
atext missing
end
for i ulong 64
arep 122 65535
end
ret afin
end
fn malbigm to int
an = bigargv true
put pa an 0
en = envone
r = execfds pa 0 add an 1 pe 0 en pk 0 0
ret 98
end
fn lyingm to int
an = achild 0 0
put pe 0 255
put pe 1 255
put pe 2 3
put pe 3 0
put pe 4 65
put pe 5 61
put pe 6 49
put pe 7 66
put pe 8 66
r = execfds pa 0 an pe 0 9 pk 0 0
ret 98
end
fn bigokm to int
clean
prep 1
kini
kadd 7
an = bigargv false
en = envone
wt sbytes
wn an
wt sp
wn en
wt sp
wn klen
wt nl
r = execfds pa 0 an pe 0 en pk 0 klen
if ne r neg long 2
ret 1
end
ret 0
end
note fork; RLIMIT_AS soft 16 MiB; execfds of the big missing-program packet, malformed by kind: 0 valid,
note 1 a trailing byte, 2 a zero byte at the end of the last record, 3 an empty first record, 4 an environment
note whose second record is empty. Returns the child's exit: 0 when execfds returned want.
fn tryas kind ulong want long to ulong
pid = fork
if lt pid 0
ret 1001
end
if eq pid 0
r = prlimit 0 9 lim 0 16
if ne r 0
exit 77
end
p64 0 16777216
r = prlimit 0 9 lim 0 32
if ne r 0
exit 77
end
an = bigargv false
if eq kind 1
put pa an 0
an = add an 1
end
if eq kind 2
put pa sub an 1 0
end
if eq kind 3
aini
ahdr 0
for i ulong 64
arep 122 65535
end
an = afin
end
en = envone
if eq kind 4
eini
etext aone
ehdr 0
en = efin
end
r = execfds pa 0 an pe 0 en pk 0 0
if ne r want
exit 1
end
exit 0
end
ret reap pid
end

note ---- parent ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
fn main to int
if ge argcnt 2
if argis 1 cmode
ret childm
end
if argis 1 smode
ret statusm
end
if argis 1 nmode
ret countm
end
if argis 1 gmode
ret rangem
end
if argis 1 rmode
ret reportm
end
if argis 1 fmode
ret faultm
end
if argis 1 pmode
ret packetm
end
if argis 1 lmode
ret launchm
end
if argis 1 omode
ret orderm
end
if argis 1 snapmode
ret snapm
end
if argis 1 mbmode
ret malbigm
end
if argis 1 lymode
ret lyingm
end
if argis 1 bomode
ret bigokm
end
ret 36
end
clean
note 1-2: status descriptor through a pipe
r = pipefds pb 0 8 524288
if ne r 0
ret 1
end
pr = int rd32 0
pw = int rd32 4
pid = fork
if lt pid 0
ret 1
end
if eq pid 0
r = dupfd pw 7 524288
if lt r 0
exit 97
end
nullat 9 0
aini
aself
atext smode
anum 7
an = afin
en = envone
kini
kadd 7
r = execfds pa 0 an pe 0 en pk 0 klen
exit 98
end
c = fclose pw
if ne reap pid 0
ret 1
end
n = read pr rb 0 len rb
if ne n long len okmsg
ret 2
end
for i ulong len okmsg
if ne get rb i get okmsg i
ret 2
end
end
n = read pr rb 0 len rb
if ne n 0
ret 2
end
c = fclose pr
en = envone
note 3: both kept descriptors were opened O_CLOEXEC
an = achild 7 9
kini
kadd 7
kadd 9
if ne tryl 2 an en klen 0
ret 3
end
note 4: descriptor 3 is a valid entry
an = achild 3 0
kini
kadd 3
if ne tryl 3 an en klen 0
ret 4
end
note 5: empty keep list
an = achild 0 0
kini
if ne tryl 1 an en 0 0
ret 5
end
note 6: failed exec closes the unlisted, keeps the listed
aini
atext missing
an = afin
kini
kadd 7
if ne tryr an en klen neg long 2 false 0
ret 6
end
note 7: a kept descriptor that is not open: -9, nothing closed
an = achild 7 0
c = fclose 40
kini
kadd 7
kadd 40
if ne tryr an en klen neg long 9 true 0
ret 7
end
note 8: the largest descriptor number is inside the range
kini
kadd 2147483647
if ne tryr an en klen neg long 9 true 0
ret 8
end
note 9-14: invalid keep lists trap 3
kini
kadd 7
if ne tryl 1 an en 2 103
ret 9
end
put pk 4 0
if ne tryl 1 an en 5 103
ret 10
end
kini
kadd 9
kadd 7
if ne tryl 1 an en klen 103
ret 11
end
kini
kadd 7
kadd 7
if ne tryl 1 an en klen 103
ret 12
end
kini
kadd 2
if ne tryl 1 an en klen 103
ret 13
end
kini
kadd 2147483648
if ne tryl 1 an en klen 103
ret 14
end
note 15: list order is checked before any descriptor is
kini
kadd 40
kadd 7
if ne tryl 1 an en klen 103
ret 15
end
note 16: packet framing is checked before any descriptor is
kini
kadd 40
put pa 0 0
put pa 1 0
if ne tryl 1 2 en klen 103
ret 16
end
note 17-21: malformed packets trap 3 (keep [7])
kini
kadd 7
put pa 0 1
put pa 1 0
put pa 2 0
put pa 3 0
if ne tryl 1 4 en klen 103
ret 17
end
an = achild 7 0
put pa an 0
if ne tryl 1 add an 1 en klen 103
ret 18
end
put pe 0 0
put pe 1 0
if ne tryl 1 an 2 klen 103
ret 19
end
put pe 0 2
put pe 1 0
put pe 2 3
put pe 3 0
put pe 4 65
put pe 5 61
put pe 6 49
put pe 7 0
put pe 8 0
if ne tryl 1 an 9 klen 103
ret 20
end
put pe 0 1
put pe 1 0
put pe 2 3
put pe 3 0
put pe 4 65
put pe 5 0
put pe 6 49
if ne tryl 1 an 7 klen 103
ret 21
end
note 22: argv and environment past the old exec caps reach the child
aini
aself
atext nmode
anum 1100
anum 73
for i ulong 1095
arep 120 1
end
arep 121 65535
an = afin
eini
etext dupe
etext dupe
ebig 5000
emany 70
en = efin
kini
if ne tryl 0 an en 0 0
ret 22
end
